course: dictionary
lesson: 10319
title: Tracker: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tracker can be a person, a device, a chart, or even hidden code. You do not need to know every meaning before you start. Read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Scientists tied tiny trackers to hornets, found and destroyed the nests» tells you a tracker here is a small device, because scientists tie things to hornets and then find them.
explain: Look for the clue words. «Scientists put small GPS trackers on storks and found they use the same routes as their parents» has GPS and routes, so the tracker is a device that shows where a bird goes. The famous trackers who read footprints and signs are people, so the word can also mean someone who follows tracks.
explain: Always test your meaning. Swap in your idea and check it still makes sense. In «reading tracker», the word tracker must mean a chart that follows your progress, because you can fill it in each day.
fact: A tracker is a noun: a tracker, trackers.
fact: Meaning 1: a person who follows the tracks or signs of animals or people.
fact: Meaning 2: a device or app that shows where something is, like a GPS tracker or a fitness tracker.
fact: Meaning 3: a chart or list for following progress, like a reading tracker.
fact: Meaning 4: on the internet, a hidden piece of code on a website that records what you do.
exercise: «Scientists put small GPS trackers on storks and found they use the same routes.» What is a GPS tracker here? | A person who reads footprints | A nest built high in a tree | *A small device that shows where the stork is | A bird's song
exercise: Dad checks the parcel tracker to see where his delivery is. What kind of tracker is it? | *A device or app that shows where something is | A chart of reading progress | A person who follows animal tracks
exercise: Mia fills in her reading tracker every night. What does it do? | *It is a chart that follows her progress | It is a hidden code on a website | It counts the steps she walks | It is a person who follows footprints
test: «Trackers showed cuckoos crossing the Sahara in one flight lasting days.» In this sentence, what do the trackers do? | *Show where the cuckoos go | Hide the cuckoos from hunters | Count the eggs in the nest | Teach the cuckoos to sing
test: In the nature lessons, the famous Aboriginal Australian and Native American trackers were good at what? | Painting pictures of the sky | Cutting hair | *Reading footprints and signs | Baking bread over a fire
exam: Which sentence uses tracker to mean a hidden piece of code on a website? | Mia coloured in her reading tracker chart | Dad's fitness tracker counted 8,000 steps today | *Websites use trackers to record what visitors do online | The tracker followed the lion's paw prints across the sand
